      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The synthesis and structure-activity relationship (SAR) study of a novel series of N-type calcium channel blockers are described. L-Cysteine derivative 2a was found to be a potent and selective N-type calcium channel blocker with IC(50) 0.63 microM on IMR-32 assay. Compound 2a showed analgesic efficacy in the rat formalin-induced pain model by intrathecal and oral administration."},
